(a) Residential lots may have a maximum of two business vehicles. Residential lots may have a maximum of two recreational vehicle(s) provided that no such recreational vehicle exceeds a length of 45 feet and that each is stored or parked completely within a garage or carport, or in the side or rear yard on a driveway or parking area constructed of concrete, asphalt, grasscrete, or other impervious surface at least as wide and long as the vehicle. Any parking area shall be directly adjacent to a paved driveway. The recreational vehicle may be connected to an outlet but may not be occupied. The setback for a recreational vehicle shall be five feet on the side yard and ten feet in the rear yard. A recreational vehicle may not be parked or stored where it would constitute a clear and demonstrable vehicular traffic hazard or be a threat to the public health or safety.
